{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "How I built the chat application for my blog.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f8c8ba35f3abf396ba09ef9d3ec2346d569a2440b10881269ccb769d10835b02.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.2, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.5], [3, 0.5, 0.64], [4, 0.64, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 2.04], [7, 2.04, 2.2], [8, 2.2, 2.5]]}, {"text": "I have been chatting on wizpert offering technical support for questions and I was inspired to add a chatting aspect to my blog.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/815d684a19b4d786f44db48ea34575811ca3dd6488e4c5068b3ddb72bb651375.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.8], [4, 0.8, 1.02], [6, 1.44, 1.76], [7, 1.76, 2.1], [8, 2.1, 2.58], [9, 2.58, 2.78], [10, 2.78, 3.22], [12, 3.58, 3.66], [13, 3.66, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.24], [15, 4.24, 4.46], [16, 4.46, 4.62], [17, 4.62, 4.74], [18, 4.74, 5.04], [19, 5.04, 5.4], [20, 5.4, 5.66], [21, 5.66, 5.78], [22, 5.78, 6.04]]}, {"text": "Feel free to hit me up on any Javascript, Ruby on Rails, or general programming questions.", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5cfc7cf6542678d333f6bb91c5520eca53a72119c14ff25a77833473db57336c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 0.98], [5, 0.98, 1.2], [6, 1.2, 1.3], [7, 1.3, 1.58], [8, 1.58, 2.14], [9, 2.14, 2.58], [10, 2.58, 2.84], [11, 2.84, 3.1], [12, 3.1, 3.76], [13, 3.76, 4.08], [14, 4.08, 4.6], [15, 4.6, 5.06]]}, {"text": "Installing NodeJS v0.10.26 on OSX Maverick 10.9", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4c67ec0c5f4d010a256439b21e1a1e0ad346abacf8ac26f2e6821600f608fd7d.mp3"}, {"text": "I recommend installing this application with homebrew, so you can easily update it as you need to.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b5b862084ebde3cbdfcfc30b9acf1ded291bffb06859bf46bb1459bcc0d5ce8d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 1.0], [3, 1.0, 1.28], [4, 1.28, 1.72], [5, 1.72, 2.1], [6, 2.1, 2.52], [7, 2.52, 2.88], [8, 2.88, 2.98], [9, 2.98, 3.1], [10, 3.1, 3.42], [11, 3.42, 3.84], [12, 3.84, 4.04], [13, 4.04, 4.24], [14, 4.24, 4.38], [15, 4.38, 4.54], [16, 4.54, 4.76]]}, {"text": "```console install nodejs brew update brew doctor brew install node", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/033833d18ae5baf7fb268bd672395376a289443fed6d1df3fe794449e1c3433a.mp3"}, {"text": "Creating the NodeJS chat server", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/887dbe3dd7b3ee792dea625ae17c906994e86c7115611de818ae8ed9f040c9d2.mp3"}, {"text": "I create all of the singleton variables at the top of the nodejs file.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0bf133b6b7c966c4be96ffb2c027049720c92829b44678b4f4ba2b8870887c41.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 0.9], [5, 0.9, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 2.04], [8, 2.04, 2.14], [9, 2.14, 2.34], [10, 2.34, 2.54], [11, 2.54, 2.62], [13, 3.08, 3.44]]}, {"text": "xmpp is used for connecting to Google Talk.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e8aa41fcb79655742b42372c2d0d5af56324bed443d410a112cb48e81ac0243b.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.5, 0.82], [2, 0.82, 1.08], [3, 1.08, 1.3], [4, 1.3, 1.68], [5, 1.68, 1.94], [6, 1.94, 2.18], [7, 2.18, 2.54]]}, {"text": "app, server, and io are used to host the server and talk with the client via sockets.io.", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b6ef08ee48013fdc6de77766a47f0077d7b623d00263922c00f08ac60cae2cbf.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.36], [1, 0.56, 0.8], [3, 1.24, 1.6], [4, 1.6, 1.92], [5, 1.92, 2.12], [6, 2.12, 2.32], [7, 2.32, 2.54], [8, 2.54, 2.68], [9, 2.68, 3.0], [10, 3.0, 3.24], [11, 3.24, 3.46], [12, 3.46, 3.64], [13, 3.64, 3.74], [14, 3.74, 4.1], [15, 4.1, 4.36]]}, {"text": "I need to keep track of what admins are connected and what users are connected.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5bd862cc5ae9d3f38e35f64782df10d7713bcad68f40dc7e48e8324616ff1140.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.4], [3, 0.4, 0.56], [4, 0.56, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.06], [6, 1.06, 1.16], [7, 1.16, 1.62], [8, 1.62, 1.7], [9, 1.7, 2.1], [10, 2.1, 2.4], [11, 2.4, 2.56], [12, 2.56, 2.86], [13, 2.86, 3.08], [14, 3.08, 3.46]]}, {"text": "While there will only be one admin account, they can be logged into multiple locations.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/92334b9b9f8c66b944b22e0981aa430002fa9590e64ef1be2ae0dadf65c761c7.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.46], [3, 0.46, 0.66], [4, 0.66, 0.82], [5, 0.82, 1.06], [6, 1.06, 1.44], [7, 1.44, 1.82], [8, 2.04, 2.12], [9, 2.12, 2.26], [10, 2.26, 2.38], [11, 2.38, 2.6], [12, 2.6, 2.86], [13, 2.86, 3.22], [14, 3.22, 3.82]]}, {"text": "For users, I need to keep track of their socket and their names to send to the client.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8f6c9a75d0abc16fca7d7f0bd07c49473a9172fd48eb8d9e68c8f4138fb02ac0.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.14, 0.52], [3, 1.1, 1.24], [4, 1.24, 1.34], [5, 1.34, 1.44], [6, 1.44, 1.72], [7, 1.72, 1.9], [8, 1.9, 2.04], [9, 2.04, 2.42], [10, 2.42, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 2.82], [12, 2.82, 3.1], [13, 3.1, 3.34], [14, 3.34, 3.54], [15, 3.54, 3.72], [16, 3.72, 3.82], [17, 3.82, 4.12]]}, {"text": "These will both be hash arrays keyed on their socket.id.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/cd9070770b03c9d3f29324b8dfe635bc639f21653fd8dfd24b8fc2afff2a209e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.42], [2, 0.42, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.78], [5, 1.1, 1.34], [6, 1.34, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 1.82], [8, 1.82, 1.96]]}, {"text": "server.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000); tells the server to listen to the hosting port.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/58125063e9d3e76cf45b78a41a1c4a61827c59bc28ee3de892cb35c3f7ecbcb6.mp3"}, {"text": "Heroku wants to set its own report, so you must try to environment report before you use the development port (3000).", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/808a098c65160dfda2b0d83edfcd44e4ea82688db1aa82c5db29d19eae7fe1c2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.44], [1, 0.44, 0.72], [2, 0.72, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.1], [4, 1.1, 1.3], [5, 1.3, 1.52], [6, 1.52, 1.92], [7, 2.38, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.6], [9, 2.6, 2.82], [10, 2.82, 3.14], [11, 3.14, 3.34], [12, 3.34, 3.8], [13, 3.8, 4.2], [14, 4.2, 4.58], [15, 4.58, 4.82], [16, 4.82, 5.06], [17, 5.06, 5.18], [18, 5.18, 5.54], [19, 5.54, 5.92]]}, {"text": "Once a socket has connected, we send them a welcome message via chat.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/d2e46da80837124481dd69b37b922c9912e93f8714565d5d06ca2513411b218d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [2, 0.36, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.82], [4, 0.82, 1.26], [5, 1.76, 1.84], [6, 1.84, 2.02], [7, 2.02, 2.18], [8, 2.18, 2.26], [9, 2.26, 2.52], [10, 2.52, 2.92], [11, 2.92, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.56]]}, {"text": "This also contains where or not the admin is available to talk.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/98c57b00892f1274fad4583f33ae36f38172c8c3954089aceff408d50e312d7c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.5], [2, 0.5, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 1.18], [4, 1.18, 1.38], [5, 1.38, 1.56], [6, 1.56, 1.74], [7, 1.74, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.22], [9, 2.22, 2.52], [10, 2.52, 2.74], [11, 2.74, 2.94]]}, {"text": "When an admin connects, we add them to the registered admins list and set the admin socket on the users hash to the admin socket so when a client messages, we will know which admin socket to send it to.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/f339c955b521440bb389ca2df2d0861efee8e99f6e8337288bfd322ab87a35c6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 1.06], [4, 1.5, 1.6], [5, 1.6, 1.8], [6, 1.8, 1.98], [7, 1.98, 2.1], [8, 2.1, 2.22], [9, 2.22, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 3.24], [11, 3.24, 3.4], [12, 3.4, 3.74], [13, 3.74, 3.94], [14, 3.94, 4.14], [15, 4.14, 4.42], [16, 4.42, 4.86], [17, 4.86, 5.1], [18, 5.1, 5.22], [19, 5.22, 5.72], [20, 5.72, 5.84], [21, 5.84, 6.12], [22, 6.12, 6.26], [23, 6.26, 6.52], [24, 6.52, 6.96], [25, 7.26, 7.3], [26, 7.3, 7.48], [27, 7.48, 7.58], [28, 7.58, 7.88], [29, 7.88, 8.26], [30, 8.7, 8.92], [31, 8.92, 9.04], [32, 9.04, 9.24], [33, 9.24, 9.54], [34, 9.54, 9.92], [35, 9.92, 10.28], [36, 10.28, 10.52], [37, 10.52, 10.72], [38, 10.72, 10.9], [39, 10.9, 11.1]]}, {"text": "Each socket represents its own chat session with a client.", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/725b87123d87668a679b99f08986efeff458106a785f65d96336c14eb83e3675.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.32], [1, 0.32, 0.66], [2, 0.66, 1.16], [3, 1.16, 1.44], [4, 1.44, 1.6], [5, 1.6, 1.84], [6, 1.84, 2.2], [7, 2.2, 2.38], [9, 2.48, 2.8]]}, {"text": "When the server gets a message from the admin, it runs the admin_to_server event and it transmits the message to the client and back to the admin.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/b4d5b9ca51e3d307b18cc91f35d432bb3a39ebd137cc6df698190577f6b11652.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 0.96], [5, 0.96, 1.22], [6, 1.22, 1.46], [7, 1.46, 1.64], [8, 1.64, 1.96], [9, 2.38, 2.46], [10, 2.46, 2.68], [11, 2.68, 2.92], [14, 5.82, 6.06], [15, 6.06, 6.16], [16, 6.16, 6.74], [17, 6.74, 6.88], [18, 6.88, 7.16], [19, 7.16, 7.4], [20, 7.4, 7.48], [21, 7.48, 7.84], [22, 7.84, 8.1], [23, 8.1, 8.28], [24, 8.28, 8.5], [25, 8.5, 8.62], [26, 8.62, 8.96]]}, {"text": "This way both users can see the message.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bdd7cca7544758566fa310c34666ec6542005713fbf706148b2f6c9c09691dfc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.62], [3, 0.62, 0.92], [4, 0.92, 1.16], [5, 1.16, 1.34], [6, 1.34, 1.48], [7, 1.48, 1.76]]}, {"text": "Clients trigger the message_to_server action when they want to send a chat message to the admin.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/cfdce1b14137c9a29b4bb1ea6632df8860101f28f14553c9a9f7ba2822d14b08.mp3"}, {"text": "If we haven’t seen this user before, we add them to the users hash and spit their message back to them.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8c5bea4ced04f7b51341db3b8d08b430d9f762f714b9934b753cbf0da4ef35fb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.36], [2, 0.36, 0.66], [3, 0.66, 0.88], [4, 0.88, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.32], [6, 1.32, 1.74], [7, 2.22, 2.36], [8, 2.36, 2.52], [9, 2.52, 2.72], [10, 2.72, 2.9], [11, 2.9, 3.02], [12, 3.02, 3.38], [13, 3.38, 3.54], [14, 3.54, 3.94], [15, 3.94, 4.2], [16, 4.2, 4.4], [17, 4.4, 4.68], [18, 4.68, 4.96], [19, 4.96, 5.18], [20, 5.18, 5.38]]}, {"text": "If the admin hasn’t connected yet, it sends a xmpp message to the admin’s gmail account notifying them that they someone is interested in talking with them.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ef4b6aa174dd872d31f961ed36725cd38a67e6180b92d4f7a74eb304fe33d078.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.26], [5, 1.26, 1.64], [6, 2.0, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.22], [10, 3.04, 3.38], [11, 3.38, 3.68], [12, 3.68, 3.8], [13, 3.8, 4.26], [14, 4.26, 4.44], [15, 4.44, 4.92], [16, 5.32, 5.84], [17, 5.84, 6.06], [19, 6.28, 6.42], [20, 6.42, 6.82], [21, 6.82, 7.02], [22, 7.02, 7.44], [23, 7.44, 7.62], [24, 7.62, 7.92], [25, 7.92, 8.12], [26, 8.12, 8.38]]}, {"text": "The URL in the message contains the user’s socket so the server will know what admin socket is intended for what user.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8e0e0ada7900759a88d466f5144f07f7e1f8ce4c9af624a37ab6103babb5abb5.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.92], [3, 0.92, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.3], [5, 1.3, 1.74], [6, 1.74, 2.02], [7, 2.02, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.74], [9, 2.96, 3.02], [10, 3.02, 3.14], [11, 3.14, 3.44], [12, 3.44, 3.62], [13, 3.62, 3.8], [14, 3.8, 4.02], [16, 4.3, 4.68], [17, 4.68, 4.94], [18, 4.94, 5.26], [19, 5.26, 5.54], [20, 5.54, 5.7], [21, 5.7, 6.06]]}, {"text": "If the admin has connected, then it transmits it to their socket.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4a55292626eec205f0d4bbf128f68dce5b72d0a1309175276546a3168855097d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.68], [3, 0.68, 0.92], [4, 0.92, 1.4], [5, 1.76, 1.86], [6, 1.86, 1.98], [7, 1.98, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.6], [9, 2.6, 2.74], [10, 2.74, 2.88], [11, 2.88, 3.26]]}, {"text": "We need to keep track of when the admin is available for contact.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/84c6d0e018f5d2cfa70d6e842e24f1f9b4bff3073dd4a011ccb98bd5d2e811f2.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.42], [3, 0.42, 0.56], [4, 0.56, 0.82], [5, 0.82, 0.98], [6, 0.98, 1.08], [7, 1.08, 1.24], [8, 1.24, 1.48], [9, 1.48, 1.7], [10, 1.7, 2.02], [11, 2.02, 2.28], [12, 2.28, 2.68]]}, {"text": "When the server starts, it initiates an xmpp connection and starts getting notifications about contact statuses.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5e9a843819305ea89bd18370881570fb8a023a52f3d87d0260770a91ea790157.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.98], [4, 1.3, 1.5], [5, 1.5, 2.08], [6, 2.08, 2.22], [7, 2.22, 3.02], [8, 3.02, 3.32], [9, 3.32, 3.8], [10, 3.8, 4.1], [11, 4.1, 4.3], [12, 4.3, 5.0], [13, 5.0, 5.42], [14, 5.42, 5.8], [15, 5.8, 6.6]]}, {"text": "If a user changes status or logs in, we add the admin to the adminXMPP so we know who to contact when a client arrives.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/35d5f3bffb19737b6ca6d796fef8a57b642621f1aac2e4824d2cc5307c0b0533.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.92], [4, 0.92, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.58], [8, 2.42, 2.52], [9, 2.52, 2.64], [10, 2.64, 2.8], [11, 2.8, 3.1], [12, 3.1, 3.32], [13, 3.32, 3.46], [15, 4.66, 4.98], [16, 4.98, 5.14], [17, 5.14, 5.32], [18, 5.32, 5.52], [19, 5.52, 5.62], [20, 5.62, 6.08], [21, 6.08, 6.36], [22, 6.36, 6.46], [23, 6.46, 6.7], [24, 6.7, 7.0]]}, {"text": "If they log out, they are removed from adminXMPP.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/186bd5abfb7638fccb6e394f1d854fccd437c5d254e96bfff440c4315d7463fa.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.9], [4, 1.12, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.3], [6, 1.3, 1.62], [7, 1.62, 2.02]]}, {"text": "If the length of the array is 0, no admins are available and we report that to clients.", "block": 14, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4e38797eba17fed07b905a3dc523e457228cab150a6f17e011a60abd521de492.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 0.88], [5, 0.88, 1.08], [6, 1.08, 1.32], [8, 2.2, 2.3], [9, 2.3, 2.74], [10, 2.74, 2.9], [11, 2.9, 3.26], [12, 3.26, 3.54], [13, 3.54, 3.66], [14, 3.66, 3.94], [15, 3.94, 4.16], [16, 4.16, 4.34], [17, 4.34, 4.66]]}, {"text": "The status message is set to ‘SparkBot is ready’ when the xmpp client connects and it displays their user information in the logs.", "block": 15, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/334a8bc24a84be1ece5da148e5f447fff12e71af6d81c90159858232db092e29.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.88], [3, 0.88, 1.1], [6, 1.52, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.46], [8, 2.46, 2.72], [9, 2.72, 3.04], [10, 3.04, 3.2], [13, 3.98, 4.28], [14, 4.28, 4.64], [15, 4.64, 4.74], [16, 4.74, 5.1], [17, 5.1, 5.34], [18, 5.34, 5.58], [19, 5.58, 6.14], [20, 6.14, 6.34], [21, 6.34, 6.44], [22, 6.44, 6.72]]}, {"text": "If there are any errors with the xmpp client, they are displayed in the logs and the process is killed.", "block": 16, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e2c5f7b451438a83b16981f293f75c34e5d07d69f1445eb3e5b94ace9321cff0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.26], [1, 0.26, 0.4], [2, 0.4, 0.54], [3, 0.54, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 1.04], [5, 1.04, 1.22], [6, 1.22, 1.4], [8, 1.9, 2.48], [9, 2.88, 3.1], [10, 3.1, 3.12], [11, 3.12, 3.46], [12, 3.46, 3.64], [13, 3.64, 3.74], [14, 3.74, 4.04], [15, 4.04, 4.26], [16, 4.26, 4.36], [17, 4.36, 4.72], [18, 4.72, 4.96], [19, 4.96, 5.28]]}, {"text": "The set_status_method function wraps the xmpp request to set the status message for the Google Talk client.sdfsdf", "block": 17, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/00f534fc3f27083832b75119e9020320b6aa00c4d62f40015805b027032ba376.mp3"}, {"text": "Creating the Client view", "block": 18, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8f23cee3b2f4175fbfc9bc8aee0267f4dd74ede131ad8b97d4beee9893de7970.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 1.04]]}, {"text": "This blog is hosted on Github Pages and talks with my server on a different subdomain (chat.kcoleman.me).", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ba6aca290f75782263275845f5e2ba01d783d2ded0f383725d3a12086c04378a.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.64], [3, 0.64, 0.94], [4, 0.94, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.46], [7, 1.94, 2.26], [8, 2.26, 2.52], [9, 2.52, 2.72], [10, 2.72, 2.88], [11, 2.88, 3.2], [12, 3.2, 3.46], [13, 3.46, 3.58], [14, 3.58, 3.86], [15, 3.86, 4.52]]}, {"text": "I loved the style of Google Talk’s chat window with the speech boxes pointing to a profile pic.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ffc3481358deddbe70c83c560208e08731b781af72e130b37f3fc93667ed2fbc.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.52], [2, 0.52, 0.74], [3, 0.74, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.32], [5, 1.32, 1.56], [6, 1.56, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.3], [8, 2.3, 2.64], [9, 2.64, 2.88], [10, 2.88, 3.0], [11, 3.0, 3.3], [12, 3.3, 3.66], [13, 3.66, 4.04], [14, 4.04, 4.34], [15, 4.34, 4.44], [16, 4.44, 4.74]]}, {"text": "Since I don’t have a profile pic to use, I replaced that with a name.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5124d7545d2b731fac6ed002ce18f64a08bbf5268a0582e94b7b82e0f5edc90f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 0.82], [5, 0.82, 1.2], [7, 1.48, 1.7], [8, 1.7, 1.92], [9, 2.34, 2.4], [10, 2.4, 2.7], [11, 2.7, 3.0], [12, 3.0, 3.18], [13, 3.18, 3.28], [14, 3.28, 3.5]]}, {"text": "You can style this code to your hearts content, but the Javascript I used looks like this.", "block": 19, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/dc76ec3ff5d4e59fc18cd228b7165b97bd7cbabd74c7de51659fcff1197f1ec3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.7], [3, 0.7, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.2], [5, 1.2, 1.38], [6, 1.38, 1.5], [7, 1.5, 1.88], [8, 1.88, 2.18], [9, 2.54, 2.66], [10, 2.66, 2.78], [11, 2.78, 3.2], [12, 3.2, 3.52], [13, 3.52, 3.86], [14, 3.86, 4.14], [15, 4.14, 4.38], [16, 4.38, 4.62]]}, {"text": "It first tries to connect to the server.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/051298b77074a77eb34ce235333e880378cab969e239f31ca69035fb26153c6c.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.24, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.8], [3, 0.8, 0.98], [4, 0.98, 1.22], [5, 1.22, 1.5], [6, 1.5, 1.6], [7, 1.6, 1.88]]}, {"text": "When it receives a message to display, the message_to_client action is triggered.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a78fbb56416236d56633bcd02415a591a845475eb3a0cbe1b6489445621290ff.mp3"}, {"text": "Here I format the HTML as a string based off of the data payload.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/59a09ccbcb628fc6c2df28cc28c488048ff445ec4de6f7097d3bb57324397553.mp3"}, {"text": "Then it adds into the discussion window.", "block": 20, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0e248df4651ed2f00ec68ea6826abf40445d4662dcde1de9f362e1d3dbc95574.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.84], [3, 0.84, 1.2], [4, 1.2, 1.38], [5, 1.38, 1.8], [6, 1.8, 2.18]]}, {"text": "When a user clicks the submit button, I get the values of the input name and message box and send them to the server as “message_to_server” and then clear the box for the next message.", "block": 21, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5f9aef582c23278642f1fe2a11f2ae798205430e731e1f418c0f2d9ecaaf29ca.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.34], [2, 0.34, 0.6], [3, 0.6, 0.86], [4, 0.86, 1.08], [5, 1.08, 1.34], [6, 1.34, 1.66], [7, 2.12, 2.18], [8, 2.18, 2.3], [9, 2.3, 2.44], [10, 2.44, 2.78], [11, 2.78, 3.0], [12, 3.0, 3.14], [13, 3.14, 3.4], [14, 3.4, 3.68], [15, 3.68, 4.02], [16, 4.02, 4.26], [17, 4.26, 4.58], [18, 4.58, 5.22], [19, 5.22, 5.42], [20, 5.42, 5.62], [21, 5.62, 5.76], [22, 5.76, 5.86], [23, 5.86, 6.16], [24, 6.16, 6.6], [27, 8.68, 8.82], [28, 8.82, 9.14], [29, 9.14, 9.36], [30, 9.36, 9.56], [31, 9.56, 9.8], [32, 9.8, 9.92], [33, 9.92, 10.14], [34, 10.14, 10.62]]}, {"text": "Because this uses Sockets.io, we need to include their library in the client as well.", "block": 22, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/0cfb02df644a8d62876034d05d17d0884b2518949bb7490e57cc91d71ba2937c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.3], [1, 0.3, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.88], [4, 2.34, 2.42], [5, 2.42, 2.54], [6, 2.54, 2.7], [7, 2.7, 3.0], [8, 3.0, 3.2], [9, 3.2, 3.66], [10, 3.66, 3.86], [11, 3.86, 3.94], [12, 3.94, 4.24], [13, 4.24, 4.46], [14, 4.46, 4.68]]}, {"text": "Creating the Admin View", "block": 23, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fd8483443fd7b0a3137c575e5e4061d739cbcff2ac68582a619cbf6b1275222e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.46], [1, 0.46, 0.68], [2, 0.68, 1.0], [3, 1.0, 1.34]]}, {"text": "This code should look pretty similar to the client, except we need the admin to register right when it connects so we can start sending him the client messages.", "block": 24, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/090ac7bd3acc6ab416f91e2644e5204fcfef51dad668e55d5d6e7692f1a01c34.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.0], [4, 1.0, 1.26], [5, 1.26, 1.62], [6, 1.62, 1.84], [7, 1.84, 1.96], [8, 1.96, 2.28], [9, 2.68, 2.94], [10, 2.94, 3.18], [11, 3.18, 3.32], [12, 3.32, 3.5], [13, 3.5, 3.78], [14, 3.78, 4.04], [15, 4.04, 4.4], [16, 4.4, 4.7], [17, 4.7, 4.88], [18, 4.88, 5.0], [19, 5.0, 5.3], [20, 5.3, 5.58], [21, 5.58, 5.68], [22, 5.68, 5.82], [23, 5.82, 6.04], [24, 6.04, 6.36], [25, 6.36, 6.6], [26, 6.6, 6.76], [27, 6.76, 7.04], [28, 7.04, 7.46]]}, {"text": "```javascript admin page var socketio = io.connect(“chat.kcoleman.me”); register();", "block": 25, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/728b7f15b26260f9d55418166d180f3514c7c2771439727bc9522e4b5153478d.mp3"}, {"text": "var target_user = document.URL.substring(document.URL.indexOf(“#”)+1); socketio.on(“message_to_client”, function(data) { document.getElementById(“chatlog”).innerHTML = (“<hr/>” + data[“name”] + “: “+ data[‘message’] + document.getElementById(“chatlog”).innerHTML); });", "block": 26, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1a8b7e1f1efe49dc9c15f437da179532efaa439a79c37e56e19756872a918eab.mp3"}, {"text": "function register() { socketio.emit(“admin_signin”, { user_id: target_user }); }", "block": 27, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3fabefcadc03fbb8c33bedfaabf3d39e1884fbf51dafbcfa3eb0ee13b9a419a4.mp3"}, {"text": "function sendMessage() { var msg = document.getElementById(“message_input”).value; socketio.emit(“admin_to_server”, { message : msg, socket_id : target_user}); document.getElementById(“message_input”).value = “”; } ``` When the client connects, it immediately tries to register itself so that the system will know it is available to receive messages.", "block": 28, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/fb129307c44b4b04d325b1f702c8904109be7f80e960d056afe83039f3eb0599.mp3"}, {"text": "In the Future", "block": 29, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c36093f8d0c817c3f4369b1f658f46ba7b1cd3307b4fc92a436aa7d71a52a796.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.3], [2, 0.3, 0.6]]}, {"text": "I want to be able to retrieve the client’s user agent so if there are any browser compatibility errors, I can easily see what browser they have.", "block": 30, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/54974d4dedd43f7b03b3735368d85733596d94779e9479dc4e6d7a270ced222c.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.44], [3, 0.44, 0.54], [4, 0.54, 0.72], [5, 0.72, 0.9], [6, 0.9, 1.28], [7, 1.28, 1.5], [8, 1.5, 2.0], [9, 2.0, 2.22], [10, 2.22, 2.56], [11, 2.56, 2.86], [12, 2.86, 3.06], [13, 3.06, 3.2], [14, 3.2, 3.34], [15, 3.34, 3.62], [16, 3.62, 3.94], [17, 3.94, 4.64], [18, 4.64, 5.14], [19, 5.48, 5.78], [20, 5.78, 5.92], [21, 5.92, 6.24], [22, 6.24, 6.54], [23, 6.54, 6.72], [24, 6.72, 7.04], [25, 7.04, 7.26], [26, 7.26, 7.64]]}, {"text": "If there is a strong need, I may look at implementing a co-browsing solution so I will be able to follow along with them as they navigate my website.", "block": 30, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/96716d7d83ea6290be90ae66d36b222b73a7039ae63f001bf3a1008ff8434962.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.4], [3, 0.4, 0.5], [4, 0.5, 0.76], [5, 0.76, 1.1], [6, 1.8, 1.86], [7, 1.86, 2.0], [8, 2.0, 2.2], [9, 2.2, 2.3], [10, 2.3, 2.74], [11, 2.74, 3.0], [13, 3.6, 4.14], [14, 4.38, 4.44], [15, 4.44, 4.6], [16, 4.6, 4.7], [17, 4.7, 4.82], [18, 4.82, 5.04], [19, 5.04, 5.18], [20, 5.18, 5.46], [21, 5.46, 5.8], [22, 5.8, 6.0], [23, 6.0, 6.22], [24, 6.22, 6.42], [25, 6.42, 6.56], [26, 6.56, 6.86], [27, 6.86, 7.14], [28, 7.14, 7.56]]}]}